  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Arkansas has recorded $69.6M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date, spread across 362 awards with an average award size of $192K. Obligations are down 94.7% year over year. Federal buying in Arkansas remains concentrated: the Department of Veterans Affairs accounts for $42.9M of obligations, while the next-largest buyers are the Department of Justice with $8.8M and the Department of Energy with $5.6M. Contracting in FY2027 to date is focused on construction, medical services, and food manufacturing industries, led by Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction at $14.2M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $10.4M. BRISTON CONSTRUCTION, LLC is the largest vendor with $14.2M, followed by JETT'S SPECIALTY CONTRACTING, LLC at $10.2M and PAFFORD MEDICAL SERVICES, INC. at $6.4M. Historical context shows federal obligations to Arkansas ranged from $1.3B to $2.1B in FY22 through FY26, with FY27 at $69.6M so far and the current-year totals partial because the fiscal year is in progress.",
    "sections": [
